---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InquiryForm from '../components/InquiryForm.astro';
import ServiceArtwork from '../components/ServiceArtwork.astro';
import ProcessArtwork from '../components/ProcessArtwork.astro';
import ExtrasArtwork from '../components/ExtrasArtwork.astro';
import '../styles/services.css';
import '../styles/services-page.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Business Services | Cloud & Capital" description="Cloud, AI and software cost reviews for growing tech teams, plus workflow reviews and tool setup for service businesses. Defined scope and clear next steps with Diana Molski.">
  <main id="main-content" class="offer-page business-services">
    <section class="services-shell services-hero" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <div class="services-hero-copy">
        <p class="service-kicker">Business services · Cloud &amp; Capital</p>
        <h1 id="services-title">Your tools should<br /><em>earn their keep.</em></h1>
        <p class="services-lede">Understand growing technology costs. Improve recurring work. Build the tool you need.</p>
        <p class="services-aside">Because another subscription isn’t always the answer.</p>
        <div class="services-actions"><a class="offer-button" href="#offers">Explore the services <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="service-text-link" href="#inquiry">Ask me about your business →</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="services-hero-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="hero" /></div>
    </section>
    <section id="offers" class="services-shell offers-section" aria-labelledby="offers-title">
      <div class="services-section-heading"><div><p class="service-kicker">Three ways to work together</p><h2 id="offers-title">A useful place to start.</h2></div><p>For growing tech teams managing rising costs, and service businesses improving how work gets done.</p></div>
      <div class="service-cards">
        <article id="technology-cost-review" class="service-card cost-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="cost" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">01 · Understand the spending</p><h3><span>Technology</span> Cost Review</h3><p class="service-question">“Why are our technology costs growing?”</p><p>For startups and growing tech teams with meaningful cloud, AI, and software spend. Understand what is driving costs and what deserves attention before you scale.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>A reconciled cost baseline and growth drivers</li><li>Cost per workload or result where records support it</li><li>A prioritized action plan and next checks</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; example</summary><p>A defined set of cloud accounts, AI workloads, or software vendors, usually covering three recent billing months. We agree the systems, records, and question before quoting. Review cost drivers, ownership, usage, commitments, and growth scenarios where the evidence supports them.</p><p>Architecture changes, migrations, and account changes are separate. Complex allocation or commitment analysis needs its own agreed scope. If a few low-cost subscriptions are the whole question, start with the free renewal worksheet.</p><a href="/services/examples#cost">See a fictional cost review →</a></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a cost review <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
        <article id="workflow-review" class="service-card workflow-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="workflow" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">02 · Understand the work</p><h3><span>AI &amp; Workflow</span> Review</h3><p class="service-question">“Why does this take so long?”</p><p>For service businesses repeatedly moving information between emails, documents, and spreadsheets. Get a plan for one recurring task, including whether AI or automation belongs in it.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>A map of where work gets stuck</li><li>A recommended change, with costs and tradeoffs</li><li>A scoped implementation plan with success checks</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; example</summary><p>One workflow across up to three tools, using two or three redacted examples. We compare simpler processes, existing features, automation, and AI—including costs, checking, and maintenance.</p><p>Your pilot plan includes a success measure and an owner. You can use it independently; building it is separately scoped.</p><a href="/services/examples#workflow">See a fictional workflow review →</a></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a workflow review <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
        <article id="practical-setup" class="service-card setup-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="setup" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">03 · Put the change to work</p><h3><span>Tool &amp;</span> Automation Setup</h3><p class="service-question">“Can you help me build it?”</p><p>For a business with a clear project: a reporting template, connected tools, or a small automation built and checked. Book directly when you know what you need.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>The agreed setup, ready to use</li><li>Checks for normal use and exceptions</li><li>Instructions and a proper handoff</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; approach</summary><p>One agreed result across up to three compatible tools, individually quoted. We agree the inputs, deliverable, tests, and maintenance owner before work starts.</p><p>A paid review isn’t required when the project is clear. New features and ongoing support are agreed separately.</p></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a setup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="service-choice-note">Growing costs <em>and</em> recurring work? Or not sure where to start? <a href="#inquiry">Tell me what’s happening.</a> We’ll find the right starting point before paid work.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="services-method" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <div class="services-shell">
        <div class="method-heading"><p class="service-kicker">A clear scope, from the start</p><h2 id="process-title">Here’s how we work.</h2><p>Start with an email. We’ll take it from there.</p></div>
        <ol class="method-steps">
          <li><div class="method-visual"><ProcessArtwork kind="email" /><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span></div><h3>Tell me what’s stuck.</h3><p>The question, the tools, and what you’d like to change. A few lines are enough.</p></li>
          <li><div class="method-visual"><ProcessArtwork kind="scope" /><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span></div><h3>Agree on the plan.</h3><p>You’ll know the deliverable, fixed quote, and timeline before we begin.</p></li>
          <li><div class="method-visual"><ProcessArtwork kind="handoff" /><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span></div><h3>Put it to use.</h3><p>Actionable recommendations or a working setup—with a handoff so you know what comes next.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="services-shell services-about" aria-labelledby="reviewer-title"><div class="services-portrait"><img src="/images/diana-molski-portrait.png" alt="Diana Molski, founder of Cloud & Capital" width="820" height="806" loading="lazy" /><p>Diana Molski · Los Angeles</p></div><div><p class="service-kicker">Your reviewer &amp; builder</p><h2 id="reviewer-title">Hi, I’m Diana.<br /><em>I like a good money question.</em></h2><p>I studied finance and worked in wealth management at Morgan Stanley. Today I combine finance and FinOps analysis with tools that help teams understand technology costs and improve the work behind their reports.</p><p>I like asking the slightly annoying questions: What is this costing? Who uses it? And why are we doing it this way?</p><ul class="services-credentials" aria-label="Professional credentials"><li>FinOps Practitioner &amp; FOCUS Analyst</li><li>AWS Cloud Practitioner</li><li>Azure AI Fundamentals</li></ul><a class="service-text-link" href="/#about">More about my background →</a></div></section>
    <section class="services-proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title"><div class="services-shell proof-grid"><div><p class="service-kicker">Built by Cloud &amp; Capital</p><h2 id="proof-title">Tools that make<br /><em>numbers easier to use.</em></h2><p>AI Cost Lens compares the cost behind a usable AI result. Cloud Cost Guard brings cloud, AI, and software spending into view.</p><a class="service-text-link" href="/tools">Explore the tools →</a></div><figure><a href="https://lens.cloudandcapital.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Explore AI Cost Lens"><img src="/images/ai-cost-lens-cost-anatomy-wide.png" alt="AI Cost Lens screen comparing model, infrastructure, and human review costs" width="2048" height="901" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>AI Cost Lens · Illustrative tool example, not a client result.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
    <section class="services-shell services-extras" aria-label="Resources and education">
      <a class="extra-panel checklist-panel" href="/resources/software-renewal"><div class="extra-copy"><p class="service-kicker">Free checklist</p><h3>Before you renew<br /><em>that software.</em></h3><p>Eight questions to help you decide whether it’s worth keeping.</p><span class="service-text-link">Get the checklist →</span></div><ExtrasArtwork kind="renewal" /></a>
      <a class="extra-panel lessons-panel" href="/learn"><div class="extra-copy"><p class="service-kicker">One-to-one lessons</p><h3>Investing &amp; trading,<br /><em>explained.</em></h3><p>From investing basics to understanding a trading setup. Start with your questions.</p><span class="service-text-link">Explore the lessons →</span></div><ExtrasArtwork kind="markets" /></a>
    </section>
    <section class="services-shell services-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="service-kicker">FAQs</p><h2 id="faq-title">Before<br /><em>you book.</em></h2></div><div><details><summary>What will it cost?</summary><p>You receive a defined scope and fixed quote before work begins. Setup fees depend on the result and systems involved.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to buy new software?</summary><p>Existing tools and simpler processes are considered first. Any proposed external cost is made explicit.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need a review before booking setup?</summary><p>No. You can book setup directly when the result and scope are clear. A review helps when you need to decide what to change, and its recommendations are yours to use independently.</p></details><details><summary>Is a paid cost review right for my business?</summary><p>It fits when technology spending, growth, or complexity makes the decision worth investigating. A few inexpensive subscriptions usually don’t justify a paid cost review. Start with the free worksheet; reporting or manual-work problems may fit a different service.</p></details><details><summary>Are savings guaranteed?</summary><p>Findings explain evidence and assumptions. Time freed up is kept separate from cash savings; the recommendation may be to keep your existing system.</p></details></div></section>
    <section id="inquiry" class="services-contact" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title"><div class="services-shell services-contact-grid"><div><p class="service-kicker">Let’s start with your question</p><h2 id="inquiry-title">What’s getting<br /><em>stuck?</em></h2><p>A few lines are enough. You don’t need to choose a service first.</p><p>I’ll reply with any questions, then a scope and quote if there’s a useful project.</p><p class="contact-privacy">Leave out financial records, passwords, and sensitive client information.</p></div><InquiryForm kind="business" /></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
